From 6850da1c460b3cfa3892a92e5561e6f99cc62f80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grzegorz <grzegorz2047@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:46:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: Honour predication for buffer copies.

D3D12 predicates CopyBufferRegion and CopyResource, but
VK_EXT_conditional_rendering does not apply to transfer commands, so
predicated buffer copies always ran. While a predicate is set, buffer
copies now go through a meta compute shader (cs_copy_buffer, BDA, byte
granular with masked edge words) whose dispatch is predicated like any
other, through conditional rendering or the indirect fallback. Copies
without a predicate still use vkCmdCopyBuffer2.

ClearState also ends conditional rendering before it forgets the
predicate.

Found with XCL's console SetPredicationBufferX test, which failed on
vkd3d-proton ("EQUAL_ZERO(0) must skip dst[0]") and passes with this on
an RTX 3060. Texture copies, tiles and resolves are not covered yet.
New test: test_conditional_rendering_copy_buffer (CopyBufferRegion with
aligned and unaligned ranges, CopyResource); not run here, the vkd3d
test suite is not built in this tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
